Subject: [PATCH] C13, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M19; main's
 fourth folder, items 1 and 2): THE RECORD READ FOR SELECTION AND CHIRALITY IS
 THE ARC B1905, WITH ITS LOCK, AND MAIN'S RULE IS IN THE WORKING RULES

Main read the record for what it settled on selection and on chirality, and wrote the arc's page, its verdict
file, its rows, its lists and its script. This patch places them as the arc, as the arcs before it, and
writes the lock. THE PAGE, THE VERDICT LINE, EVERY NUMBER AND THE RULE ARE MAIN'S, AND NONE IS REWORDED. The
classes in the rows are the readers', one reader an arc; nothing here checks them.

WHAT IS PLACED. frontier/B1905_selection_and_chirality_across_the_record/: main's page and verdict file from
its drafts, byte for byte; under verification/, main's rows, its lists of arcs, its script, its kept table
and its kept run, byte for byte. The folder main handed over keeps its copies. The rule, in main's words from
that folder, is a new section at the end of WORKING_RULES.md. The status page has a line for the arc, made of
the verdict line's own sentences.

THE LOCK, ten tests.
  - The rows and the lists are the files main gave, by their digests, and are the same files as in the
    folder main handed over.
  - The tables are what main's script makes of the rows; the kept table says the same, and the kept run
    gives the same numbers.
  - EVERY NUMBER OF THE PAGE AND OF THE VERDICT LINE STANDS IN A SENTENCE THAT IS BUILT FROM THE ROWS, and
    the sentence is looked for: 30 sentences, among them the fifteen rows of the page's two tables, the
    counts of the sweep, the counts of the split by words, the seven pairs, and the verdict line's walls and
    shares. A digit alone is held nowhere.
  - The 1,644 arcs are counted at the commit the readers read.
  - Every quotation is looked for at that commit, by main's own function: 547 of 547, controls 0, as main
    kept. WHERE THE COMMIT IS NOT IN THE CLONE the test is skipped and says so in capitals, and a test that
    needs no commit holds that the kept table was made with it.
  - Main's two plants fail. A quotation changed: the digest sees it, and main's function names the arc. A
    class changed (one arc moved from the first wall to the second): the digest, the tables, and the
    sentences of the page and of the verdict line each see it. A number changed on the page or in the line,
    with the rows as they are, is seen too.
  - The rule's section in the working rules is main's by its digest, and is the block of main's folder.

The lock runs none of main's script as a process. The script writes its kept table at every run; the lock
reads the script, compiles it without an import and calls its functions, so a test leaves the checkout as
it found it.

MADE AGAIN BEFORE IT WAS PLACED, as the card asks: every number of the page and of the verdict line comes
out of the rows as main states it. Nothing differed.

WHAT GOES BACK TO MAIN (it is in the series' note as well).
  1. The page's table of walls gives five of the eight classes. The three it leaves out (a scale or
     hierarchy, 17; an identification borrowed, 28; other, 32) hold 77 of the 511. The heading says 511 and
     the table's rows sum to 434. The page is not touched.
  2. 184 of the 636 rows give no date.
  3. The verdict is PROVED for a reading of the record; that is main's.
  4. Main's script writes its kept table at every run. Whether it writes on request only is main's.

Every gate passes but the count of landings, which is past 40 on this base. The lock, the test of verdict
files and the 16 test files that read the working rules or the status page: 1,718 passed. Built on main's 1e8ef44de with
R80b's parts 2 to 5 built again there. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session
that wrote the lock.

THE HAND-OVER FOLDER LEAVES THE TREE WITH ITS ARC (main's M27): docs/handoffs/MAIN_TO_BUILDER_2026-11-12_D/ is removed
in this patch, and docs/REORGANIZATIONS.md's entry of 2026-11-13 says so in a line. Its files are in git's history at
9c8a50887, the commit the entry names. B1905's lock compared its rows, lists, script and rule with main's copies in the
folder; it now reads them there, with git show, and holds that the folder is gone. The move script's check says the tree
is as moved.
